this morning amnesty international says  russian authorities may be slowly trying  to kill  president vladimir putin's most public  critic alexi navalny is a prisoner  inside a russian penal colony and his  supporters say  navalny suffers from severe pain and is  being denied medical treatment  our holly williams now has the latest on  the efforts to see him  even behind bars alexei navalny is  causing trouble for the russian  government  russian police detained nine people  yesterday when his supporters  including his personal physician tried  to gain access to navalny in prison  i'm very really very afraid of his  health and  his condition that's why i'm here now do  you trust the prison doctor no  navalny started a hunger strike a week  ago a protest against the russian  authorities denying him access to his  doctors  the outspoken opponent of the russian  government says he's suffering from  acute leg  and back pain navalny was sentenced to  two and a half years behind bars in  february for violating parole  a case his supporters say was  politically motivated  it followed his near-fatal poisoning  last august  with the nerve agent novichok which  navalny blames on russia's leaders  a russian government source recently  released this cctv footage of navalny in  prison  the russian authorities say he's  receiving all necessary  medical assistance alexey navalny's  lawyer says he's lost  28 pounds since he was locked up and is  suffering from sleep deprivation  anthony ali williams in london thank you  holly
 

